+# Jobs 5.2.6.3 Excel XP candidate
+
+This is an off-server paired candidate, not a live installation or an upstream version upgrade.
+
+## Provenance
+
+- Upstream: https://github.com/Zrips/Jobs
+- Exact base tag: `v5.2.6.3`
+- Exact base commit: `6fe3c272c3c970d4a94fbf7615953803eb722503`
+- Plugin name remains `Jobs`.
+- Candidate version: `5.2.6.3-Excel-XP-1`.
+- Preserve the upstream Apache/GPL license files and complete corresponding source when distributing a candidate JAR.
+
+## Why an XP-event listener alone is insufficient
+
+In the pinned upstream `Jobs.java`, normal `action` consumes the final
+`JobsExpGainEvent.getExp()` value, then caches it in `FASTPAYMENT` and applies it
+to `JobProgression.addExperience`.
+
+The cached `perform` path captures XP before its events and adds that old value to
+progression even after listeners change XP. Its displayed/logged XP can therefore
+differ from real progression. Changing that one local variable alone is also
+insufficient: cached XP already includes native and external event boosts, so
+repeating those boosts would compound them.
+
+The cached path is used by rapid same-material block breaks and the
+`payForAbove` block-physics path for sugar cane, bamboo, kelp and weeping vines.
+Ordinary gameplay rewards funnel through `Jobs.action`. Administrative
+`/jobs exp` and `/jobs grantxp` directly alter progression and intentionally do
+not receive gameplay Together/weekend bonuses.
+
+Sources:
+
+- https://github.com/Zrips/Jobs/blob/v5.2.6.3/src/main/java/com/gamingmesh/jobs/Jobs.java
+- https://github.com/Zrips/Jobs/blob/v5.2.6.3/src/main/java/com/gamingmesh/jobs/listeners/JobsPaymentListener.java
+- https://github.com/Zrips/Jobs/blob/v5.2.6.3/src/main/java/com/gamingmesh/jobs/container/JobProgression.java
+- https://github.com/Zrips/Jobs/blob/v5.2.6.3/src/main/java/com/gamingmesh/jobs/PlayerManager.java
+
+## Narrow changes
+
+1. Discover the paired mcMMO plugin lazily through three public reflected methods:
+   `isJobsXpBonusSupported()`, `getJobsXpBonusMultiplier(Player)` and
+   `notifyJobsXpGain(Player)`. No direct mcMMO dependency or new load-order edge.
+2. Expose `Jobs.isExcelXpBonusSupported()` as the paired-build capability marker.
+3. Apply the Excel multiplier after cancellable Jobs XP events, once per award.
+   Keep this multiplier out of the replay cache.
+4. Recompute only XP on cached replay using the current job progression/formula,
+   pre-payment event, native EXP boost/minimum, and XP-gain event. This avoids
+   compounding cached native or third-party XP boosts. Cached money and points
+   retain their existing behavior.
+5. Pass one final XP value to payment reporting, logging, and actual progression.
+6. Notify mcMMO only after positive XP really raises stored XP or job level.
+   A fully capped level-200 job does not generate a false recent-XP notification.
+
+Absent, disabled, unsupported, or incompatible mcMMO leaves base XP in place.
+Non-finite, below-one, or overflowing bonus multipliers also leave base XP intact.
+Zero and negative XP are not multiplied. XP remains a double, with no new rounding.
+Asynchronous callbacks skip the optional bridge without touching its cached state.
+The three reflected methods must be instance methods returning exactly
+`boolean`, `double`, and `void`, respectively.
+
+## Preserved behavior and limits
+
+- This patch does not change money/points formulas, rewards, currency settings,
+  shop settings, data files, or saved balances. It never enables points.
+- Existing Jobs currency-limit accounting occurs before the Excel multiplier.
+  Its counters therefore consume base/event XP, not this added Excel bonus.
+  Existing cached-path limit semantics are preserved, including the upstream
+  any-currency-allowed check. This is not a currency-limit redesign.
+- Normal XP-event cancellation still suppresses XP while preserving money/points;
+  cached XP-event cancellation still cancels the entire cached payment, matching
+  upstream. Pre-payment cancellation remains honored in both paths.
+- Real `JobProgression` level-up and maximum-level clamps remain authoritative.
+- A cached replay with a missing job/action or configured maximum-level payment
+  stop cannot award XP; existing cached money/points behavior is left alone.
+- No direct administrative XP grants or Minecraft green-XP changes are added here.
+
+## Verification required before deployment
+
+The JUnit regression suite executes the real patched `Jobs.action` and
+`Jobs.perform` methods plus real `JobProgression`. It checks actual stored XP,
+not only event values or displayed payment text. It covers cached replays,
+third-party/native multipliers, solo/Together/weekend/combined factors,
+cancellation, fractional and nonpositive XP, level-up and caps, malformed bridge
+values, optional-plugin discovery, eligibility and unchanged money/points.
+
+Run these tests with JDK 21 using the full upstream Maven build when its optional
+dependency repositories are available. The public repository also supplies a
+standalone bridge-only test harness that does not compile the award paths.
+Do not substitute the cached JitPack `v5.2.6.2` artifact for an exact 5.2.6.3
+baseline: its embedded version is `5.2.6.1`.
+
+No live server checks or installation are implied by an off-server test pass.
+
+### Candidate verification on 2026-10-12
+
+- PASS: standalone real bridge Java compilation and 22 JUnit cases, offline with
+  cached Paper API 1.21.4, JDK 21, JUnit 5.11.4 and Mockito 5.15.2. Zero failures,
+  errors or skipped cases. Mockito is supplied as a startup Java agent, avoiding
+  restricted dynamic-attach behavior.
+- NOT RUN: full real-Jobs award suite and baseline-failure comparison. These
+  require the full upstream dependency set or a separately validated focused
+  build against exact baseline binaries. Required dependencies were unavailable
+  because of repository-access failures.
+- NOT BUILT: deployable paired Jobs candidate JAR. The build pipeline refuses to
+  create one until the full real-Jobs tests succeed against verified inputs.
+- NOT PERFORMED: live server installation or gameplay validation.
